name 'building-data-driven-systems-preassessment-q9_2025'

question 'A developer is building a weather app. How should they structure the data to store a 7-day forecast where each day has a high temperature, low temperature, and condition?'

wrong 'Seven separate variables named `day1`, `day2`, etc.'
wrong 'A single string containing all the numbers for the week.'
right 'An array of 7 objects, where each object contains the high, low, and condition'
wrong 'An object containing 7 different arrays of numbers.'

allow_multiple_attempts true

teacher_markdown <<MARKDOWN
Lesson 5

An array of objects is the standard way to store a list (the 7 days) of complex items (the specific forecast details for each day).
MARKDOWN
